 @yvindvego9404  If you mean to speak of something like you understand it, learn it first.
"The half-power point or half-power bandwidth is the point at which the output power has dropped to half of its peak value; that is, at a level of approximately -3 dB" 

Also, my 5700 XT Pulse is quiet as a mouse, but i use custom curves, anything else is amateur.

 @MonicaHolly143  That motherboard is great for at least a 3900X and any GPU you could desire to put in it, and the 3600 is  a great CPU even for higher end GPU's, although going beyond an RTX2080S is a little unbalanced, but the CPU will still keep up with it.

I definitely would not get an RTX2060 for RT (raytracing), the performance is really bad and you'll be better off waiting for more powerful GPU's for RT if that matters to you, even an RTX 2070S is pretty weak for it.

Driver stability on RX5000 series GPU's should be mostly resolved now, but there is always a risk that those issues may affect you or could return in the future, so if you're at all worried that the drivers could be a problem then NVidia might be the better option for you.

